Newspeak3
'Test'
(* newspeak-spec.pdf 3.1.1: "An object is a value object if it is deeply
   immutable ... and its class inherits from class Value." A mutable slot
   is state something can write after the fact, so a class below `Value`
   that declares one could never have a value object for an instance --
   and a value that could change would stop being equal to the copy an
   actor boundary made of it.

   The refusal is an ordinary Newspeak error raised where the instance
   would come into being, so the line before it still prints: nothing about
   the class is wrong until something asks for an instance of it.

   The module is a value (`Object <: Value`) because §3.1.1 asks a value
   class's enclosing object to be one; the transcript is therefore read
   from `platform` where it is used, never held in a slot. *)
class ValueMutableSlot usingPlatform: platformAtCreation = Object <: Value () (
    public class Counter = Value new (
        | public count ::= 1. |
    ) ()
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        platform transcript show: 'before'; newLine.
        platform transcript show: Counter new printString; newLine.
    )
) : ()
